    {
      "id": "seed-de-la-riva",
      "type": "position",
      "label": "De La Riva",
      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "Keep it SHALLOW - deep DLR demands hip rotation, hamstring tolerance and inversion that do not fit your attributes. Weight forward -> sideways sweep; controlled leg moves back -> stand-up foot sweep; sits back -> lapel sweep; posts a hand after being pulled -> SLX; knee-cuts or drops a hip beside you -> Octopus.",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-12T21:19:39.060Z"
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "tags": [
        "bottom",
        "gi"
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "DLR",
        "Shallow DLR"
      ],
      "variantOf": "seed-open-guard",
      "category": "Guards",
      "fromPositionId": null,
      "toPositionId": null
    },
    {
      "id": "seed-knee-shield",
      "type": "position",
      "label": "Knee Shield Half Guard",
      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "Tier-1 bottom hub vs kneeling/pressure opponents. Direction A (they stay square): protect the crossface, underhook, onto your side, dogfight. Direction B (they hip-switch or turn away): clear the arm, sit up, Octopus Guard. The dilemma: face you and give up the underhook game, or turn away and give up Octopus.",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-12T21:19:39.060Z"
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "tags": [
        "bottom"
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "Z-Guard"
      ],
      "variantOf": "seed-half-guard",
      "category": "Guards",
      "fromPositionId": null,
      "toPositionId": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ebg-octopus",
      "type": "position",
      "label": "Octopus Guard",
      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "Tier-1 reaction guard (Telles; Gi-specific system exists). Available when they hip-switch, turn hips away during a knee cut, reach for a crossface, reverse-kesa or sit heavily beside you. Control checklist: keep one leg trapped in half guard, clear the crossface arm past your centreline, SIT UP (not on your shoulder), wrap the far lat/waist/belt, chest attached to their back or rear shoulder, head above their shoulder, posting hand free. Get behind their shoulder line, not just around the waist. Attack order: 1 back take, 2 kosoto hip-bump, 3 wrestle-up, 4 butterfly sweep, 5 recover knee shield (a branch, not a failure).",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-12T21:19:39.060Z"
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "tags": [
        "bottom",
        "gi"
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "Octopus Half Guard"
      ],
      "variantOf": null,
      "category": "Guards",
      "fromPositionId": null,
      "toPositionId": null
    },
    {
